# Noble Cascade — Code ownership for security-critical areas.
#
# Repository teams are placeholders until the owner creates them; replace
# @noble-cascade/<team> with the real team slugs. Until then, every rule also
# requires a human maintainer review via branch protection (see
# docs/maintainer-security-checklist.md — "requires maintainer action").
#
# Ownership domains:
#   governance  — trust model, security spec, certification, release evidence
#   runtime     — execution kernel, ledger, replay, audit
#   sandbox     — process boundary, execution limits
#   policy      — scope/auth policy, worker definitions, config schemas
#   workers     — trusted built-in tools
#   ci          — workflows, verification scripts, dependency automation
#   release     — release machinery, attestations, SBOM/provenance

# Governance (security specification is the trust root of all guarantees)
/docs/security-spec.json               @noble-cascade/governance
/docs/guarantee-matrix.md              @noble-cascade/governance
/docs/governance-proof.md              @noble-cascade/governance
/docs/repository-governance.md         @noble-cascade/governance
/docs/maintainer-security-checklist.md @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/certify.py                      @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/trust_report.py                 @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/trust_index.py                  @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/governance.py                   @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/spec.py                         @noble-cascade/governance
/noble/compliance.py                   @noble-cascade/governance

